<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.head(
      title: "For sales teams — CSuiteFinder",
      description: "$#{@seat_usd} per person per month, and every month that seat gets $#{@seat_usd} of lookup credit. Verified work emails and direct numbers for the people you need to reach.",
      nav: :teams,
      audience: :sales,
      css: CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.page_css(:teams)
    ) %>
<header>
  <h1>Your team reaches the decision-maker. Not the contact form.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Give a name and a company, get a verified work email and a direct number.
    No API key, no terminal, and no meter running while you work.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-cta">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/account#pricing">Start a seat — $<%= @seat_usd %>/month</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/account">Try it free first</a>
  </div>
  <p class="cta-note">
    <%= @trial_usd %> of credit, no card, good for <%= @trial_months %> month.
    Run your own list through it before deciding anything.
  </p>
</header>

<h2 class="section-label">What your team actually does with it</h2>

<div class="does">
  <div class="item"><strong>Work a target account</strong><span>Give us the company domain and get the people at it, filtered to executives — names, titles and addresses.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Reach a named person</strong><span>You know who you need. We work out their address from how their company formats email.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Get a direct number</strong><span>A mobile or direct line for the same person, with the carrier and line type.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Check before you send</strong><span>Every address verified against the live mailbox, so bounces never touch your sending reputation.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Know who called</strong><span>A number you were called from, matched back to the person and their company.</span></div>
</div>

<h2 class="section-label">Why the addresses are good</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  Over 95% of lookups resolve, and every address can be verified against the live
  mailbox before anyone sends to it. That check is included, and it is the single
  best thing you can do for your domain's inbox rate: a bounced cold email costs
  you far more than the lookup did.
</p>

<h2 class="section-label">How the monthly credit works</h2>

<div class="step"><span class="step-n">1</span><div><strong>You are billed $<%= @seat_usd %> a month per seat.</strong> Through PayPal, on the same day each month, until you stop it.</div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">2</span><div><strong>Each payment tops the account up to $<%= @seat_usd %> a seat.</strong> That is what the lookups draw down — around <%= @seat_emails %> work emails, or <%= @seat_phones %> phone numbers, or any mix of the two.</div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">3</span><div><strong>Whatever is left at the end of the month goes.</strong> The next payment starts you at $<%= @seat_usd %> again rather than $<%= @seat_usd %> plus the remainder.</div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">4</span><div><strong>A lookup that finds nothing costs nothing.</strong> You are only ever charged for an answer.</div></div>

<!-- ── pricing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     At the foot of the page on purpose: the nav's Pricing link is a bare
     #pricing fragment, so it scrolls down this page rather than sending a
     salesperson to the developer plan. -->
<h2 class="section-label" id="pricing">Pricing</h2>

<div class="plan">
  <div>
    <span class="price">$<%= @seat_usd %></span><span class="per">per person, per month</span>
  </div>
  <p class="gets">
    Every seat gets <strong>$<%= @seat_usd %> of lookup credit</strong> each month.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <%= for item <- @seat_includes do %>
    <li><%= item %></li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <ul class="caveats">
    <%= for item <- @seat_caveats do %>
    <li><%= item %></li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:24px 0 0">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/account#pricing">Start a seat</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:<%= @contact_email %>">Talk to us about a team</a>
  </p>
</div>

<p class="quiet">
  Cancel any time — the month you have paid for runs to its end. There is no annual
  lock-in, because a tool worth keeping should not need one.
</p>

<p class="quiet">
  Building this into your own product rather than working in a browser? There is a
  <a href="/developers">developer plan</a> priced per answer instead.
</p>

<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.footer(:sales) %>

</div>
</body>
</html>
